{
  "abstract": "A plain-language interpretive guide to Modal Triplet Theory. The book explains the program's central picture of one connected physical ontology described through compatible projections, then follows that picture through coherence, world-in-world geometry, the shared circle, q79/Fu-Yau geometry, proto-spinors, particles, the Standard Model reconstruction, quantum theory, gravity, time, memory, and cosmology. Short technical boundaries distinguish established results, declared reconstructions, and open interpretations, while proofs remain in their focused papers.",
